# What Docker should not have to read before it starts building.
#
# Without this the context is gigabytes — `target` alone dwarfs the source —
# and every build pays to send it. Worse, a stale `web/out`, a stale
# `desktop/dist` or a macOS-built `target` copied into the image would be used
# instead of what the build makes.

target
**/node_modules
web/.next
web/out
desktop/dist
.git
.claude
.dev
.firetower
.env
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
.DS_Store
